# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# ── macOS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store

# ── Tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
*.log

# ── Mati's state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `.cache/` is where Mati keeps everything it learns on this machine. Ignore
# the directory and re-admit, by name, only what ships with every install.
.cache/*
!.cache/.gitkeep

# ⭐ MATI'S FIRST MEMORIES — the shipped build artefact, tracked on purpose.
#
# ⚠️ THE NAMES ARE NOT `mati_notes.*`, DELIBERATELY. That is the PERSONAL
# store: one person's conversations, and the θ₀ those conversations shaped. It
# is created on the first turn and belongs to whoever had that conversation;
# tracking it would put somebody's memories into every clone. These are what
# `make_ship_field` produces — the charter verbatim and four measured
# self-check rows, identical on every install — and `Mati/first_run.py`
# copies them into place when there is no store yet.
!.cache/first_memories.db

# The vocabulary that goes with the shipped checkpoint.
!.cache/qa_vocab.json

# ── Results that are outputs, not source ─────────────────────────────────────
*.npy
*.npz

# ⚠️ EVERY .npz THAT SHIPS IS RE-ADMITTED HERE, BELOW `*.npz`. Git honours the
# LAST matching rule, so an exception placed above this point is silently
# overridden — and the store would ship WITHOUT the address space its `feat`
# column is measured against, which is not a degraded install but a
# meaningless one. `git check-ignore -v <path>` names the rule that decided.
#
# The shipped checkpoint (ep40, ppl_nu=965.6) and its base θ₀:
!.cache/diag_pattern8d_shuf_final.npz
!.cache/diag_pattern8d_shuf_final_theta0.npz
# Mati's first memories travel with their own address space:
!.cache/first_memories_theta0.npz
!.cache/first_memories_theta0_address.npz
